{
  "category": "Long Tail Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its tail is so powerful that it can use it to grab a tree branch and hold itself up in the air.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives atop tall trees. When leaping from branch to branch, it deftly uses its tail for balance.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses its tail to hang on to tree branches. It uses its momentum to swing from one branch to another.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "AIPOM’s tail ends in a hand-like appendage that can be cleverly manipulated. However, because the POKéMON uses its tail so much, its real hands have become rather clumsy.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "AIPOM’s tail ends in a hand-like appendage that can be cleverly manipulated. However, because the POKéMON uses its tail so much, its real hands have become rather clumsy.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail ends with a dexterous, handlike appendage. However, because it uses the tail so much, AIPOM’s real hands have become rather clumsy.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives atop tall trees. When leaping from branch to branch, it deftly uses its tail for balance.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tail is so powerful that it can use it to grab a tree branch and hold itself up in the air.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses its tail to pluck fruits that are out of reach. Its tail is more adept than its real hands.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives atop giant trees. It wraps its tail around a branch so it won’t fall off while asleep.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives high among the treetops. It can use its tail as freely and cleverly as its hands.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
